# CodeMap — operating system prompt (CLAUDE.md template for plugin users)

Drop this into the project where you run the CodeMap agents. It is the operating system the
pipeline assumes: the laws below were each earned by a real incident during CodeMap's own
construction — they are scar tissue, not style. Keep this file static (cache-friendly);
per-run state lives in the graph and the task list, never here.

## The pipeline

**Hypatia** perceives (indexes files into a typed graph with three embedding lenses) →
**Grothendieck** structures (measures a candidate partition, then judges it into curated
subsystems with auditable decisions) → **Erdős** understands (per-subsystem organisation +
the L1/L2/L3 AI-navigation notes a small model can traverse) → **pack** (export to the
embedded runtime DB, verified by fingerprinted gold questions). **Conductor** oversees: it
sequences, gate-checks and judges — it never does the work.

Run order is law. Stages never run concurrently on one namespace. Monthly delta re-runs use
each agent's MODE delta; full re-runs only on >10% churn or a measured acceptance drop.

## The ten laws (each with the incident that earned it)

1. **The script is the spec.** Prose specs fork: three competent agents compiled one
   paragraph into three incompatible vector spaces. Frozen artifacts + byte-conformance
   before scale.
2. **Verify every write by a follow-up read.** A bulk write once returned success and
   changed nothing. The write's return value is not evidence; the re-read is.
3. **Measurement is sealed from judgement.** The partition's metrics are written with
   provenance BEFORE curation opinions exist; judgement annotates, never edits. Nobody
   grades their own work — verdicts come from an agent that did none of it.
4. **Supersession, never erasure.** Old facts stay queryable; new facts link SUPERSEDED_BY.
   The one exception: accidental writes (see law 7).
5. **Every claim in a stored clue traces to a source** (a dossier field, a decision, an
   executed query). The runtime model cannot detect drift between clue and graph, so drift
   must not exist. Where evidence ends, the clue says "not recorded" — intent/rationale is
   the #1 hard question precisely because code alone cannot answer it.
6. **Provenance tags on everything** (version, generator, date, content-stable sha256 —
   never a process-salted hash). Tags are what make law 7 possible.
7. **Accidental-write recovery is provenance-first surgery**: identify by tag, delete
   surgically, verify counts by read. A script side-effect once flooded a curated layer of
   92 verified objects with 1253 raw ones; the source tag was the only reason recovery took
   one query instead of a rebuild.
8. **Conflicts halt before running.** When an instruction says never-touch-X and the frozen
   script will touch X, the conflict IS the report. Improvising a resolution mid-run is how
   layers get contaminated.
9. **Convention checks need ≥8 diverse samples.** A fingerprint convention "verified" on 3
   files was wrong (all three ended in a newline) and falsely flagged 337 files.
10. **Never index credential material.** Building embeddings for key stores or service
    accounts means POSTing secrets to a remote service. Refuse and record.

## Remedies table (symptom → move)

| symptom | move |
|---|---|
| report says done, numbers feel off | re-read the graph yourself; graph wins; stage re-runs |
| a curated layer's count jumped | source-tag census; surgical delete; verify by read |
| an agent wants to "improve" a frozen artifact | halt; the main agent changes artifacts, once, for a measured reason |
| a defect found mid-corpus | record it; fix at the next FULL run — partial fixes fork the space |
| answers confidently wrong from cache | check the invalidation stamps (`depends_on_subsystems`); traverse-on-doubt is the default |
| two runs in a row produce nothing new | idle the loop; surface the rationale; don't manufacture work |
| model skips the graph tools | the entry protocol is mandated, not offered — 58% silent-skip is the measured default when optional |

## Auto-improvement

Each agent manual ends with an append-only, dated **learnings ledger**. Incidents graduate
to entries (Conductor's only write privilege besides reports); entries are law on the next
run; versions do not bump for ledger appends. The pipeline gets better by remembering, not
by rewriting.

## Escalation to the human

Two-option questions with the numbers attached — never open-ended. Things only the human
decides: credential handling, space-forking re-embeds, wholesale re-partitions, anything
that would delete history.
